        "raw": "[quote=\"Lowendz113\"]\n\nI know the rule book states that cards act in the orer they entered the field, but I still have some questions.&nbsp;Let&#39;s say we&#39;re playing in the sewers.I&#39;m playing Ra, you are playing AZ. You bring out your Focused Apertures in round one. On round two I bring out Imbued Fire. Now all damage is fire damage. But your card was in play first, so do you add your +1 from the Apertures before applying the effect of my card?&nbsp;Now let&#39;s say Irradiated Cyclohexane Vat comes out. Do we add our +1s to damage because our cards were out first?&nbsp;\n\n[/quote]\n\n&nbsp;\n\nThis has been discussed extensively. My apologies for not having a handy reference.\n\n&nbsp;\n\nThe rule of thumb I developed for myself based on the discussion is that one determines the type of the attack before applying any increases or reductions.\n",
